I've been thinking about this one for a while and I'm surprised I've
never seen it posted. Has it? The specifics would be a 2nd level
divination spell (clerical would be silly of course). If skilled, it
would tell you the cursed/uncursed status of eveything in your main
inventory, if basic or unskilled, just one item. Now this brings it to
the strange part: does detect curse determine if an item is blessed? if
not then you have to come up with a new set of prefixes for the
"detected" items. i.e.: 


5 daggers
4 cursed daggers
6 not cursed daggers
7 blessed daggers

The last would be done by an altar of course, the 2nd by an altar or the
spell and third by the spell and the first obviously not BUC'd in any
way. The other way is to do it exactly like an altar, but that takes the
fun out of it, as you then know which items are blessed, granted it
might be useful if there are only the 5 (?) altars in the game, but
there is that nagging nastiness of not knowing what is blessed. 


The idea is to make it possible to survive without a pet or an altar in
the early game when it's most important. Namely before one can survive
in minetown or at least lugging stuff up and down from minetown to the
entrance of the mines as I'm sure is a *big* killer of characters. 

